<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss short-time work rose in November.</title>
<headline>Swiss short-time work rose in November.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of people affected by short-time work in Switzerland rose to 14,692 in November, an increase of 2,360 from the previous month, The Federal Office for Industry and Trade said.</p>
<p>The number of work hours lost to short-time working rose by 15 percent to 798,754, compared with 631,162 hours a year ago.</p>
<p>In November 1995, 631,162 work hours were lost, affecting 10,787 workers in 1,062 firms. -- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
